ell and it's pretty slow so  hopefully apple releases a much better  one and i really hope apple puts max  safe magnets on the back of the actual  battery pack itself we are expecting  better battery life and he did say that  prices may be in a completely different  direction than expected now i don't  really know what that means but he did  translate it to it saying it will be  more expensive and the price gap between  models may change too now in my personal  opinion i think that the iphone 14  regular model will stay at the same 799  with the new 14 max at 8.99 and then  both the pro and pro max models are  gonna be a hundred dollars more  expensive than they currently are now so  eleven hundred dollars for the pro and  1200 for the pro max now moving on we  just got a huge leak concerning the  ultra wide camera on the iphone 14 pro  models this year saying that it's gonna  have bigger pixels than before which  means low light performance will be  improved now actually going to the leak  itself it's from minshakuo who is very  reliable and as for the specifics going  to mingxiquo's actual tweet he says that  the iphone 14 pro models ultrawide  cameras will upgrade to 1.5 micron size  pixels versus 1.0 on the current iphone  13 pro now if you don't know how the  pixel sizes are measured it's actually  just one side of the pixel so if it's  one micron long it's also one micron  wide so it's one square micron now going  up to 1.4  is actually going to be squared which is  1.9  square microns versus one square micron  on the current 13 pro that's basically  double the surface area of each pixel  which means almost double the amount of  light going into each pixel if you keep  the same 12 megapixel sensor size that's  going to be a huge low light improvement  now moving on it looks like we did get a  leak of the actual sticker of an iphone  14 pro model so yes that name is for  sure confirmed and that it's coming in a  white box at least the pro devices on  top of that we also have confirmation  that all iphone 14 models are going to  feature six gigabytes of ram of course  with the pro models having the faster  ram and going even further we have  confirmation that there will no longer  be a sierra blue color and there will  not be a titanium model we're going to  be keeping the stainless steel for the  pros again and interestingly dan roo did  come out and talk about the 30 watt  charger that's going to be coming out  for the iphone 14 series however he did  say that the peak power of the lightning  interface of the iphone is only 27 watts  that's the maximum and the newer higher  setting to enable 30 watt is not going  to be available so i think apple is  going to be future proofing this 30 watt  charger for next year's iphone 15 series  and beyond that will be able to accept  30 watts through the usb c port now this  right here is absolutely crazy it's  rumored that apple and global star will  be announcing satellite connectivity for  the iphone 14 lineup at the september  7th event now this is nuts but it makes  total sense because in february  globalstar announced that it acquired 17  new satellites to provide continuous  satellite services to a potential  customer which might be apple and i  think that makes total sense in terms of  this rumor because you're going to be  able to go out hiking out in the ocean  on your boat yacht whatever any place  where there's no service and you will be  able to get some satellite connectivity  just enough to make a text message or a  voice call hopefully because right now  you have to buy a satellite phone with a  subscription service and apple is just  going to kill that market now moving on  mainstream quote did say that apple has  completed hardware tests for iphone 14  satellite connectivity so they're ready  but the launch is going to depend on the  partners and if they are ready on time  so i think we're really getting this  feature now let's move on to the apple  watch series 8 lineup and we just got  some new leaks from shrimp apple pro  about what we should expect now as far  as a regular series 8 we should expect  the same 41 and 45 millimeter sizing  options no differences there we are  going to be getting an updated red color  the same packaging and contents and  plentiful supply at launch so don't  expect any supply issues or demand  issues at all shrimp apple pro did say  that the box design with the seal is  going to be staying the same except that  they added more glue underneath to make  sure that it shows that you actually  opened it and people can't kind of fake  it and re-box it or anything like that  and as far as the series 8 pro he did  say that that is coming alongside a new  se watch with no major changes for the  se but the 8 pro will have some changes  and it's going to be a surprise to  people because it's going to be a one  more thing type of announcement however  there is a caveat and a potential issue  because there are rumors saying that the  pro apple watch is not going to be  compatible with older watch bands which  means that if you made a collection of  watch bands over the years you might  have to restart all over again but don't  worry because mark german did tweet  about it saying that he believes the  apple watch pro will support older bands  though maybe they won't fit as well or  look as seamless given the size of the  new watch so basically it's technically  going to fit but it's not going to look  great so you're probably just going to  buy a pro apple watch band anyway and on  top of that we also got a leak from the  japanese website mac atakara saying that  the apple watch pro is going to be  featuring a larger 47 millimeter case  size with a flat display yes it's going  to be flat which is going to allow it to  have thinner bezels and basically a  larger display within a smaller chassis  so it doesn't look massive on your wrist  and i totally agree with that i think  it's going to look absolutely amazing  and now putting the iphone and the apple  watch aside we did get a leak from  trimmed apple pro about the air pods pro  2 and the actual feature that might be  coming with it which is going to be huge  and this might be coming at the  september 7th event i'm not exactly sure  let's hope for it but shrimp a pro did  say that the lc3 codec that was leaked  is actually not for lossless but for  normal data transmission like calling  and stuff  with lossless actually having a  completely new codec which is likely a  custom apple codec that they built for  loss lossless support on the airpods pro  2 so i think that is going to be a major  selling point for those new airpods pro  2. a lot of people are going to buy it  because the quality is going to be  absolutely insane and industry changing  and finally we got some details about  apple's ar vr headset that is going to  be launching probably within the next  year who knows maybe there's a chance  apple might give us a teaser at the  september 7th event but apple applied  for trademarks of reality one reality  pro and reality processor and felipe is  thinking that reality processor means  the new family of chips just like the a  series and the m series for the max the  r series is going to be for the arvr  headsets with reality one being the r1  chip and reality pro being the name of  the device which likely means that this  is going to be very expensive and not  meant for the consumer market so  hopefully we get a teaser of that at the  apple september event now let me know  what you're excited for down in the  comments section below because i am  extremely excited definitely subscribe  by clicking the circle above and check  out one of those two right there and  we'll see you in the next video  [Music]  [Music]

